# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local state (per-developer, not shared).
# `.claude/*`, not `.claude/`: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so a negation under one can never fire. Excluding the contents instead is
# what makes the one exception below possible.
.claude/*
# ...except the permission policy, which is a PROJECT fact, not per-developer
# state: which commands an agent may run here unattended is the same question
# for Zach, Tyler and any unattended run, and it reviews like code. Same
# reasoning as Config.getLexicon() living in source rather than a sheet.
# NOTHING ELSE under .claude/ gets un-ignored — no settings.local.json (that
# is where personal overrides belong), no transcripts, no FOCUS.md (see
# aedile/.scheduler/ for why that moved out of .claude/ entirely).
!.claude/settings.json

# Node dependencies (aedile/brain, #40). package.json + package-lock.json are
# committed; the installed tree is per-box and never committed.
node_modules/

# Voice-duel burst data. wavebucks is a PUBLIC repo and these carry verbatim
# private mailing-list messages by named krewe members. duel.mjs writes them;
# aedile/recap/duel.html stays an empty template and the filled page is
# generated outside the tree. Never commit either.
aedile/recap/pairs.json
aedile/recap/*.page.html
# Per-machine play state: sha1s of archived message bodies. No reason to publish
# which of a private list's messages have been used.
aedile/recap/.duel-used.json

# Python bytecode. ingest.test.py imports ingest.py by path, which writes it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Browser session exports. `aedile/analysis/container-cookies.py` writes a Netscape
# cookies.txt for the `kreweofvaporwave` Firefox container so `gggd` can scrape the group
# as its owner. That file is a LIVE CREDENTIAL for the krewe's Google account.
#
# It is written to /srv/vaporwave-reports/aedile/ by default, outside the repo, for exactly
# this reason. These patterns are the second line: before them, a cookie file dropped in
# the repo would have been committed, because nothing here matched a secret shape.
*cookies*.txt
*.cookies
cookies.sqlite
# The scrape's resume ledger: which topic IDs already landed in the mbox. Per-machine
# progress, not a fact about the project.
aedile/analysis/.scrape-used.json

# THE CORPUS IS PRIVATE MAIL FROM REAL PEOPLE and this repo is public (#45). The canonical
# copy lives at /srv/vaporwave-reports/obsidian-vault/mailing-list-archive/ and a
# server-local cache beside it -- never here. Before these patterns nothing in this file
# matched a corpus shape, so `messages.jsonl`, a merged corpus or an mbox dropped into the
# repo would have been committable: verified 2026-09-27 with `git check-ignore`, which is
# the check #45's third bullet asks for and it was not satisfied.
#
# Only a SYNTHETIC fixture belongs in git. If one ever needs to be tracked, name it
# explicitly with a negation rather than widening these.
*.mbox
*.mbox.gz
messages.jsonl
merged*.jsonl
*-topics.jsonl
